            <title>[LU-20977] sanity-quota test_2: hangs after project quota fstrim/force_sync, session TIMEOUT</title>
                <link>https://jira.whamcloud.com/browse/LU-20977</link>
                <project id="10000" key="LU">Lustre</project>
                    <description>&lt;p&gt;Session &lt;a href="https://testing.whamcloud.com/test_sessions/8c4c746c-c4e0-4eb8-b1b8-121d4f6ce25f" class="external-link" target="_blank" rel="nofollow noopener"&gt;https://testing.whamcloud.com/test_sessions/8c4c746c-c4e0-4eb8-b1b8-121d4f6ce25f&lt;/a&gt;&lt;br/&gt;
(review-dne-part-4, build 133644) reports sanity-quota test_2 TIMEOUT.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;The subtest log (test set &lt;a href="https://testing.whamcloud.com/test_sets/87c845f9-b76c-4460-a475-9ac04c6ef307" class="external-link" target="_blank" rel="nofollow noopener"&gt;https://testing.whamcloud.com/test_sets/87c845f9-b76c-4460-a475-9ac04c6ef307&lt;/a&gt;)&lt;br/&gt;
shows test_2 running its project-quota checks (create 2048 files,&lt;br/&gt;
exceed the inode hardlimit, delete), then issuing fstrim on all 8 OSTs&lt;br/&gt;
and lctl set_param force_sync on the MDTs, after which the log stops:&lt;br/&gt;
no further output, no PASS, no FAIL. The session's own timeout fired&lt;br/&gt;
later (219 minutes) while a different suite (sanity-dom) was running,&lt;br/&gt;
so sanity-quota itself hung in test_2 rather than the whole session&lt;br/&gt;
simply running long.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;The open tickets already linked to test_2 (&lt;a href="https://jira.whamcloud.com/browse/LU-15879" title="sanity-quota test_2: user create success, but expect EDQUOT" class="issue-link" data-issue-key="LU-15879"&gt;LU-15879&lt;/a&gt;, &lt;a href="https://jira.whamcloud.com/browse/LU-16301" title="sanity-quota test_2: project create fail, but expect success" class="issue-link" data-issue-key="LU-16301"&gt;LU-16301&lt;/a&gt;,&lt;br/&gt;
&lt;a href="https://jira.whamcloud.com/browse/LU-20585" title="sanity-quota: test_2: FAIL: group create success, but expect EDQUOT " class="issue-link" data-issue-key="LU-20585"&gt;LU-20585&lt;/a&gt;, &lt;a href="https://jira.whamcloud.com/browse/LU-9326" title="sanity-quota test_2: group create success, but expect EDQUOT" class="issue-link" data-issue-key="LU-9326"&gt;LU-9326&lt;/a&gt;) are all about a specific create/delete call&lt;br/&gt;
returning the wrong result (EDQUOT expected but not seen, or vice&lt;br/&gt;
versa); none is a run that produces no result. Rainshadow shows this&lt;br/&gt;
TIMEOUT signature ("last suite running was sanity-dom") only this once&lt;br/&gt;
in the last 30 days, unticketed.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;The patch under test (&lt;a href="https://jira.whamcloud.com/browse/LU-12669" title="FLR-EC: recover data from parity code" class="issue-link" data-issue-key="LU-12669"&gt;LU-12669&lt;/a&gt;) only touches lustre/include/cl_object.h,&lt;br/&gt;
lustre/llite/file.c, lustre/lov/lov_io.c, lustre/obdclass/cl_io.c and&lt;br/&gt;
lustre/tests/sanity-ec.sh, an EC parity-read path unconnected to quota&lt;br/&gt;
enforcement or object destroy/fstrim handling.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Raised by Patch Watcher run pw-engineer-69392-ps2-f06d1f5a7c18 on &lt;a href="https://review.whamcloud.com/69392" class="external-link" target="_blank" rel="nofollow noopener"&gt;https://review.whamcloud.com/69392&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;</description>
